{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"2d106b35-cba2-4cb0-8023-9ff464d95d45","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Summary of Causes \u0026 Fixes\n\nThe causes of both issues have been diagnosed and documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-DpyuLI/ANSWER.md):\n\n1. **Production Crash (`logs/prod-error.log`)**:\n   - **Cause**: `hidden` is a DynamoDB reserved word. In [`StoryLibrary.hide`](file:///tmp/h-DpyuLI/src/app.py#L56), using `hidden` bare inside `UpdateExpression=\"SET hidden = :h, ...\"` caused DynamoDB to fail with `ValidationException: Attribute name is a reserved keyword; reserved keyword: hidden`.\n   - **Fix**: Aliased all attributes using `#alias` placeholders mapped in `ExpressionAttributeNames`.\n\n2. **Staging Story Still Visible in Feed (`logs/bug-report.md`)**:\n   - **Cause**: In [`StoryLibrary.feed`](file:///tmp/h-DpyuLI/src/app.py#L70), the bare reserved word `hidden` was used in `ProjectionExpression=\"slug, title, hidden, published_at\"`. Unlike write expressions, DynamoDB does not throw an error for bare reserved words in a `ProjectionExpression`; it silently omits the attribute from the returned items. Consequently, `i.get(\"hidden\")` evaluated to `None`, and the feed's `not i.get(\"hidden\")` filter silently passed through hidden items.\n   - **Fix**: Aliased all attributes in `ProjectionExpression` with `ExpressionAttributeNames`.\n\n3. **Blanket Prevention \u0026 Testing**:\n   - Aliased every attribute name across all expressions in [`src/app.py`](file:///tmp/h-DpyuLI/src/app.py) (`publish`, `rename`, `hide`, `feed`, and `archive`) using `ExpressionAttributeNames`.\n   - Added integration unit tests in [`tests/test_feed.py`](file:///tmp/h-DpyuLI/tests/test_feed.py#L42-L66) to test story withdrawal via `hide()` and verify that records with `hidden: True` set directly in DynamoDB are excluded from the public feed.\n","duration_seconds":63.932363,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":143903,"output_tokens":3408,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":68202,"total_tokens":147311}}}
